<description>&lt;p&gt;Gunmen killed an immigration officer and wounded another in Niger State, while bandits assaulted a post in Borgu LGA and a Christian humanitarian worker was slain in northwest Nigeria, and a Niger lawyer was jailed for a social-media post about the army. Rival jihadist groups JNIM and IS-linked factions clashed in northwestern Nigeria and in Burkina Faso, where IS claimed over 400 JNIM fighters were killed. The United States added Nigeria to its blacklist for recruiting child soldiers, and Mali expanded its reserve force by 2,400 recruits, including 800 women. The conflict produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxQekJZS0Nab2NieDNYRjhYdU1xQXduZ1pwUGREVjdKZl96eWV1TGdrSEJPOUJVODlZdnpmVUJ4eVNFZXpxZk5zY1dESlUxWDVZSnNueXVsTVFRY0V0djFRSEtibDMyOURzT3FUaFV6ekUzejVuQVJMR2VlRGh2THZWUUI5cEtvdnZUYzg0Qm8ycUctMGVHVWo1QnRR?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxPQmFUOXdXMWtuM2RjaU43d3M4ZVAzcHJUamZNUFRWOE1aM2JEMW5pdUpGS2NJdGFCaUpKRElIeC1ld3RmOWdzV3llN0RzRU5PdlFuc1lwUXktQUoxd3BqblpyTU94dWJQWlNYOVJnTDcwQnludHVDWUhscmNNTW1ETzBkQzlKWVJKZkN1bVBZbFNPaVRVZmlOeA?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXEFVX3lxTE1TTTkyVGppeko1WEFvMmEzamUxWU9rVzBaOEh6MklzRUhjRUVaWkJidHEweHFXTDcyT2dERWt4ZDV6bG9hSVdvVWtrTXpLcVRqZjhBVUVNZ2hqdkct?oc=5&quot;&gt;International Crisis Group&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivgFBVV95cUxQQUx4eHlwNjJ0Z3JWVVlHSnVOUy1Qbkg0NWR1R1BMckgtNVhPazFRdmlKMV9RVjVkN19QUWpJVWZscGFadDY5a09LTkQyeVNsNHJJX1VIS19KZlFXWmlSUDJaQXhZSG45X29OMEJnN0hSb1NrUFVFWC1VUEFuZ1JicHU4MXdvWVVsRXNkRnRFUVBFUE5qNjdfUFNGVVh5S0FOQ3R6ek5xbnhBZHpTbHBpZXdvMkR4eThjYXhpdHlB?oc=5&quo